  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "critical",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Present risk is dominated by a property finding: the design has a paid spend capability, recursive delegation, no step/runtime/retry/sub-agent limits, a prompt that explicitly says to keep going until every row is complete, and a known set of rows that never complete. Under rubric section 5a this is an S3 property finding on consequential capabilities with the autonomy modifier, yielding critical inherent risk; there are no declared or verified controls that restore the missing spend and execution limits, so residual remains critical. Forecast remains critical because no named present control decays; the main risk is already realized in the current design. Manual validation only; scripts were not available. Missing artifacts such as runtime config, audit settings, and provider/API configuration reduced coverage on non-DoS categories but did not affect the critical tier for the documented runaway spend condition."
  },
